# Copy to .env and fill in what you actually have. Every key here is optional:
# `stocks.ingest.registry` falls back to a keyless provider, and failing that to
# the synthetic provider, so the pipeline runs end-to-end with this file absent.
# Run `py run.py providers` to see which slot resolved to what.
#
# Licence terms for every provider are audited in docs/api-terms.md. Several
# carry obligations; the notes below say which.

# --- prices (DS1 equity, DS2 index and factor proxies) ---
# yfinance needs no key and is the default. Note that yfinance is an unofficial
# client and Yahoo's API is "intended for personal use only" -- fine for this
# project, not fine for a public or commercial deployment. If this ever stops
# being personal, prices are the first thing that has to be re-sourced.
#
# Alpha Vantage is the fallback for when Yahoo rate-limits. Free tier is 25
# requests/day, so it can serve the web app but not a training sweep.
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=

# --- news retrieval (feeds DS3's synthesis) ---
# GDELT needs no key and is the default: free for any use including commercial,
# indexes worldwide news every 15 minutes, and reaches back to 2015 -- the only
# free source that can cover DS2's 12-month window at all.
# Its licence requires attribution; the web app footer carries it. Leave it there.
#
# NewsAPI needs BOTH lines below, on purpose. Its free Developer plan is
# contractually "development and testing in a development environment only, and
# cannot be used in a staging or production environment (including internally)",
# so a key alone deliberately does not enable it -- pasting a key is something
# people do while exploring, setting a flag that names the restriction is not.
# It also only reaches back 30 days, which cannot build DS2 regardless.
NEWSAPI_API_KEY=
NEWSAPI_ALLOW_NONPRODUCTION=

# --- community retrieval (feeds DS3's synthesis) ---
# Reddit app credentials (https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps -- pick "script").
# Free for non-commercial use at 100 queries/minute, but since late 2025 every
# new OAuth client goes through manual approval rather than self-service signup.
# Reddit search also cannot filter by date range, so it serves DS3 only.
# Without these the community half of DS3 is empty and only news is used.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDDIT_USER_AGENT=stocks-research/0.1 by u/your-username

# --- macro ---
# FRED is free but keyed (https://fredaccount.stlouisfed.org/apikeys).
# Supplies the numeric macro series AND the risk-free rate that every excess
# return in finance/ depends on -- worth the minute it takes to register.
# Its licence requires a specific disclaimer, which the web app footer carries
# verbatim. Do not reword it.
FRED_API_KEY=

# --- sentiment synthesis (DS3) ---
# Gemini reads the news, community, and macro corpora that GDELT and Reddit
# retrieved, and returns a fixed schema of named sentiment scores. It replaces
# three raw TF-IDF blocks with ~15 interpretable numeric features.
#
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. Without one the pipeline
# still runs -- SyntheticBriefProvider fills the same schema from a word list --
# but `bundle.synthetic` records it and /api/predict warns, because the lexicon
# fallback is not a language model and results built on it mean very little.
#
# If the key comes from a Google Cloud project rather than AI Studio, the Gemini
# API must be enabled on that project first, or every call 403s with
# SERVICE_DISABLED. `py run.py models` reports that clearly and prints the
# activation URL; enablement takes a minute or two to propagate, during which
# calls fail intermittently rather than consistently.
#
# GEMINI_MODEL: run `py run.py models` to see what your key can actually reach.
# Newest is not most available -- as measured, gemini-3.6-flash and 3.8-flash
# were returning 503 through four retries while 3.5-flash answered in 11s.
# gemini-flash-lite-latest was faster still and is worth testing if throughput
# or cost binds.
#
# Cost: roughly 10k input tokens per (symbol, as-of). A ten-symbol, three-year
# weekly sweep is on the order of $5 on flash, and $0 on a re-run since briefs
# are cached like everything else.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# GEMINI_STRICT_GROUNDING defaults to ON and you almost certainly want it there.
#
# Gemini synthesises; it never retrieves. Google Search grounding is not enabled
# and must not be -- grounded search returns *today's* index, so scoring a 2023
# as-of date would hand the model articles written after the fact.
#
# But even reading only correctly-dated documents, the model recognises them:
# give it 2023 headlines about a large-cap tech company and it may remember how
# the quarter ended. Strict grounding redacts the ticker and inferred company
# names, strips dates, shuffles document order, and instructs the model to
# assume no outside knowledge.
#
# Set to 0 and briefs get visibly richer -- and your backtest gets quietly
# inflated by lookahead that no leakage check downstream can detect. Only turn
# it off for live inference, where there is no future to leak.
GEMINI_STRICT_GROUNDING=1

# --- runtime ---
STOCKS_DATA_DIR=./data
STOCKS_CACHE_TTL_HOURS=12
STOCKS_ORIGINS=

# Skip the two Chapter 10 factor-proxy ETFs (IWD/IWF), saving two price pulls
# per bundle. The `ff_*` multifactor features are then absent from the panel.
STOCKS_DISABLE_FACTORS=
